      "id": 1,
      "text": "Angola earned its name when the federal government moved the closed Taylor Hollow post office to the area in 1855, and the town adopted the name “Angola.”",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.villageofangolany.gov/history",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The arrival of a railroad line in 1852 sparked a boom, turning Angola into a bustling hub for travelers and freight.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Angola%2C_New_York",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1873 Angola incorporated as a village, marking its formal establishment within the town of Evans.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.villageofangolany.gov/history",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
